# nsrun-xserver: the X namespaces the X server starts with. Copy to
# ~/.config/nsrun/xnamespaces; it is read when X starts, so a new name
# takes a new X session. Without the file, X starts without Xnamespace.
#
# One namespace a line: NAME [ALLOW]...
#
# `nsrun -x NAME` runs a program in the namespace NAME. Its clients see
# and reach only each other: not the other windows, the keyboard while
# another window has it, or the session's clipboard. ALLOW gives some of
# that back:
#
#   mouse-motion   pointer motion outside its own windows
#   shape          windows that are not rectangles (the SHAPE extension)
#   transparency   windows that show what is under them
#   xinput         the XInput extension: touchpad gestures, smooth scrolling
#   xkeyboard      all of XKEYBOARD, changing the keyboard map included,
#                  instead of only reading it
#
# "root" and "anon" are the server's own: the session, and clients whose
# cookie belongs to no namespace.

web
#term xinput shape
